---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--  Logging
--  (HEADER=VALUE)
--  Logging values are stored in the swCardEventLogTable, each OID entry represents each slot
--  position.  The indexing of the table works using the log header string. For example if the
--  header is "FAULT", the index OID starts with the length of the header ie 5, followed by the
--  ASCII values for each letter 70 65 85 76 84.
--  Index for "FAULT" .5.70.65.85.76.84
--  To OID for FAULT on slot 12 for swCardEventLogTable is 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.12. 5.  70.65.85.76.84
--                                                         |-------base-----------|Slt|Len|-F--A--U--L--T-|
--  An SNMP GET on this OID will return the Log value associated with FAULT for slot 12 eg "NONE" (FAULT=NONE)
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Header		: SN
--
-- MIB ref		: swCardEventLogSlotXX       .2.83.78
-- absolute OID	: 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.XX.2.83.78
-- Vary			: NO
--
-- Value(s)		: 
--				: 
-- Comments		: This log field shows the unique S&W serial number for this
--				: board instance. 
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Header		: AES
--
-- MIB ref		: swCardEventLogSlotXX       .3.65.69.83
-- absolute OID	: 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.XX.3.65.69.83
-- Vary			: YES
--
-- Value(s)		: OK:INPUT_A;INPUT_B;INPUT_C;INPUT_D
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_B;INPUT_C;INPUT_D
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_B;INPUT_C
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_B;INPUT_D
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_C;INPUT_D
--				: FAIL:INPUT_B;INPUT_C;INPUT_D
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_B
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_C
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_D
--				: FAIL:INPUT_B;INPUT_C
--				: FAIL:INPUT_B;INPUT_D
--				: FAIL:INPUT_C;INPUT_D
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A
--				: FAIL:INPUT_B
--				: FAIL:INPUT_C
--				: FAIL:INPUT_D
-- Comments		: This log field shows the detected digital audio input state.
--				: OK:INPUT_A;INPUT_B: Indicates that A,B AES pairs are present.
--				: OK:INPUT_A;INPUT_B;INPUT_C;INPUT_D: Indicates that all AES pairs are present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_B;INPUT_C;INPUT_D Indicates that no AES pairs are present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_B;INPUT_C: Indicates that AES pairs A,B,C are not present.  
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_B;INPUT_D: Indicates that AES pairs A,B,D are not present.  
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_C;INPUT_D: Indicates that AES pairs A,C,D are not present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_B;INPUT_C;INPUT_D: Indicates that AES pairs B,C,D are not present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_B: Indicates that AES pairs A,B are not present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_C: Indicates that AES pairs A,C are not present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A;INPUT_D: Indicates that AES pairs A,D are not present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_B;INPUT_C: Indicates that AES pairs B,C are not present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_B;INPUT_D: Indicates that AES pairs B,D are not present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_C;INPUT_D: Indicates that AES pairs C,D are not present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_A: Indicates that AES pair A is not present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_B: Indicates that AES pair B is not present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_C: Indicates that AES pair C is not present.
--				: FAIL:INPUT_D: Indicates that AES pair D is not present.
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Header		: EDH
--
-- MIB ref		: swCardEventLogSlotXX       .3.69.68.72
-- absolute OID	: 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.XX.3.69.68.72
-- Vary			: YES
--
-- Value(s)		: NONE
--				: OK
--				: FAIL
--				: RESET
-- Comments		: This log field shows the EDH status of the SDI
--				: input.
--				: EDH (Error Detection Handling) as specified by
--				: SMPTE RP 165-1994 and by the ITU standard ITU-R BT.1304.
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Header		: MSG
--
-- MIB ref		: swCardEventLogSlotXX       .3.77.83.71
-- absolute OID	: 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.XX.3.77.83.71
-- Vary			: YES
--
-- Value(s)		: UNIT PRESENT
--				: UNIT LOST
-- Comments		: This log field shows whether the IQ frame gateway card
--				: can communicate with this module.
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Header		: STD
--
-- MIB ref		: swCardEventLogSlotXX       .3.83.84.68
-- absolute OID	: 1.3.6.1.4.1.7995.2.6.1.1.XX.3.83.84.68
-- Vary			: YES
--
-- Value(s)		: UNKNOWN
--				: 625
--				: 525
-- Comments		: This log field shows the detected video standard of the detected SDI input.
--
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Header		: AUDIO
